1
00:00:01,320 --> 00:00:03,040
ALL DEPICTED EVENTS ARE FICTIONAL

2
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:06,680
AND FOR ENTERTAINMENT PURPOSES ONLY.
VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

3
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,120
Thee! Pun!

4
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,440
Yes. I'm safe now.

5
00:00:23,520 --> 00:00:25,040
<i>Klao.</i>

6
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:26,920
Jom was right. You lost your wits.

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:28,440
<i>Who were those two?</i>

8
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:31,520
Jom and Kaew,
companions since our youth.

9
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,640
Dearest Klao,

10
00:00:32,720 --> 00:00:34,640
my name is Lady Prayong,

11
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:36,120
Lord Phop's mother.

12
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,560
On the morrow, we shall visit the temple.

13
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:40,880
Kindly join me on this journey.

14
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:47,720
Lord Preechapiban.

15
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:51,600
Will you confess to your misdeeds?

16
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:57,680
The Legal Principles decree that

17
00:00:57,760 --> 00:01:01,880
whosoever is found guilty of bribery,

18
00:01:01,960 --> 00:01:03,720
or of engaging in corruption,

19
00:01:04,599 --> 00:01:06,720
such as the trafficking of opium,

20
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:11,280
shall receive 50 lashes
upon the back,

21
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,440
be subjected to a fourfold fine,

22
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:16,840
and condemned to a life of servitude.

23
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:23,280
My father is innocent.

24
00:01:23,360 --> 00:01:25,600
Be not so hasty in your judgment.

25
00:01:26,240 --> 00:01:28,560
He is indeed guiltless.

26
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:29,800
Cease this, son.

27
00:01:31,960 --> 00:01:33,600
If you are indeed innocent,

28
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,520
why do you remain so silent?

29
00:01:38,040 --> 00:01:39,960
Speak the truth, Father.

30
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:42,720
Quite an audacious tongue you possess.

31
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:46,120
Refrain from this outburst,

32
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:50,960
or the lash shall find you
as it did your father, Lord Preechapiban.

33
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:56,000
Bear this burden in silence now,

34
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:01,400
for the day shall come
when the truth is laid bare before all.

35
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:04,000
Escort him out.

36
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,560
Father…

37
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:25,560
Father.

38
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:28,160
Father!

39
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:30,480
Father!

40
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,040
Father!

41
00:02:37,120 --> 00:02:38,040
Father!

42
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,480
Father is no more, Master!

43
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,040
Master Klao…

44
00:02:51,720 --> 00:02:52,880
Haunted by a nightmare?

45
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:54,600
<i>This dream again.</i>

46
00:02:55,240 --> 00:02:57,640
<i>Was Klao's father a convict?</i>

47
00:02:57,720 --> 00:02:59,840
<i>Right. Back then…</i>

48
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,960
Don't!

49
00:03:02,040 --> 00:03:03,320
<i>You son of a rogue!</i>

50
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,920
<i>-Vile thing!</i>
<i>-You shall never prosper, Klao!</i>

51
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,840
Prior to his passing,
Lord Preechapiban,

52
00:03:08,920 --> 00:03:12,320
your father,
left you in my keeping.

53
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:15,800
Klao's father is dead.

54
00:03:20,520 --> 00:03:21,840
Dear me, Master.

55
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:24,600
You dreamt about your father again?

56
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,600
Klao's father…

57
00:03:27,880 --> 00:03:29,320
I mean, my father…

58
00:03:29,400 --> 00:03:31,000
What was the cause of his death?

59
00:03:36,080 --> 00:03:36,960
Chuay.

60
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:39,200
Can you please tell me about it?

61
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:42,320
Even this,

62
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:44,400
you have no recollection of, Master?

63
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:52,920
Dawn is upon us, Master.

64
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Pray, go and freshen yourself.
We must prepare to go make merit.

65
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:58,600
Let's not speak of
such grim matters.

66
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,880
What does it mean to be lashed?

67
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:10,160
Is it like being slashed
by a sword or a spear?

68
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,160
If that's the case,

69
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:15,000
it's fatal, isn't it?

70
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:19,440
Was my father a convict?

71
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:25,600
Did he really do it?

72
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,880
Chuay, please tell me.

73
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,200
I want to remember it.

74
00:04:31,640 --> 00:04:32,680
Master Klao.

75
00:04:34,680 --> 00:04:36,080
Some matters…

76
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:39,520
are best left in the shadows.

77
00:04:43,120 --> 00:04:45,920
I shall prepare a cloth

78
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:47,800
for your bath, Master.

79
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,680
That…

80
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:04,680
I think that wasn't just a dream,

81
00:05:06,320 --> 00:05:07,240
but rather

82
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:10,280
Klao's memories.

83
00:07:02,800 --> 00:07:05,120
Chuay, can you
heat up the water like you did

84
00:07:05,200 --> 00:07:07,640
back at the small manor?

85
00:07:07,720 --> 00:07:10,240
I cannot, Master.
This manor is not ours.

86
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:11,880
Klao.

87
00:07:13,120 --> 00:07:14,680
Make haste and take your bath.

88
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:17,400
We must depart for the temple
with my mother.

89
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:21,160
Well…

90
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,000
If I…

91
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:25,280
Like…

92
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:28,120
It's too cold for me.

93
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:34,360
The canal water
is warmer than in a jar.

94
00:07:34,440 --> 00:07:36,560
Disrobe and bathe at once.

95
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,480
Why do you hesitate?

96
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,400
Are you mortified by me?

97
00:08:14,480 --> 00:08:16,680
<i>Does "mortified" mean embarrassed?</i>

98
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,000
I'm not, of course!

99
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:22,960
Out of the way.

100
00:08:23,760 --> 00:08:25,320
An eagle soaring on the wind!

101
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:35,360
Don't touch me.

102
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:38,200
What have you to be shy about?

103
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,520
I'm not shy.

104
00:08:39,600 --> 00:08:42,360
I don't like physical contact
when it's cold. Stop it!

105
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,000
Take off your clothes at once.

106
00:08:55,160 --> 00:08:56,520
Dear Klao.

107
00:08:56,600 --> 00:08:58,760
You appear as vibrant and full of life

108
00:08:58,840 --> 00:09:00,920
as you did before your journey to Phichit.

109
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,400
<i>Phichit? Did Klao ever move to Phichit?</i>

110
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:08,240
Does this manor afford you restful sleep?

111
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,680
I slept nice and tight.

112
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,000
What makes you so tight?

113
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,040
Chuay.

114
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:20,200
Yes, my Lady?

115
00:09:20,280 --> 00:09:22,200
In what manner did you dress him,

116
00:09:22,280 --> 00:09:23,920
that he should cry "tight" aloud?

117
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,120
See to his attire.

118
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:29,920
Yet I have attired him perfectly, my Lady.

119
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,520
Nevertheless, I shall see to it.

120
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,520
-Hey, no need. It's okay.
-No, Master.

121
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:40,040
-I can do it myself.
-As my Lady commands.

122
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:41,960
Oh, Sai.

123
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:43,520
Yes, my Lady?

124
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:44,640
Kong.

125
00:09:45,240 --> 00:09:47,840
Ready the offerings
for the Buddha and the monks

126
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,000
upon the boat at once.

127
00:09:50,080 --> 00:09:51,320
Yes, my Lady.

128
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,480
My Lady,

129
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:08,960
I beg your permission
to offer her help.

130
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,960
Kong is rather feeble.

131
00:10:11,040 --> 00:10:12,680
I fear for our timely departure.

132
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:14,760
Kong is feeble?

133
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,640
If it be envy,

134
00:10:21,280 --> 00:10:22,960
then begone with all haste.

135
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:24,800
Yes, my Lady.

136
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:33,800
What is it that you find tight?

137
00:10:34,480 --> 00:10:35,920
Allow me to adjust it.

138
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,840
It's not tight.

139
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:45,800
I spoke in the Phichit tongue,
my Lady.

140
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:48,440
Tight means nice and cozy.

141
00:10:49,920 --> 00:10:52,280
I wanted to keep it short, my Lady.

142
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:57,000
How endearing.

143
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:00,360
Let us set forth.

144
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:02,200
The rower shall soon arrive.

145
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:23,640
Let us depart.

146
00:11:24,880 --> 00:11:26,080
Tightly.

147
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:51,840
<i>Weren't Ayutthaya's ancient temples</i>
<i>made of red brick?</i>

148
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:55,440
<i>Were they really this gorgeous</i>
<i>before the Fall of Ayutthaya?</i>

149
00:11:59,120 --> 00:12:01,000
What lingers in your thoughts?

150
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:05,360
Nothing.

151
00:12:05,440 --> 00:12:07,240
I just think that

152
00:12:07,320 --> 00:12:10,320
this is quite a stunning temple…

153
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:11,920
my Lord.

154
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:15,000
You must retain some of the memories.

155
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:18,320
Lord Preechapiban,

156
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:20,200
your father,

157
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:23,440
and I once brought
Phop and you to a revel here.

158
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,120
Auntie…

159
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:31,040
Forgive me, my Lady…

160
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:36,280
were you an acquaintance of my father?

161
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:43,640
He suffers from amnesia.

162
00:12:47,920 --> 00:12:49,920
I was more than
a mere acquaintance of his.

163
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:56,200
Your father
was a companion of His Excellency.

164
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:58,720
This explains
your recurring visits to my manor,

165
00:12:58,800 --> 00:13:00,960
and our travels in days gone by,

166
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:04,920
until…

167
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,800
your relocation to Phichit in his company,
when that incident occurred.

168
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:19,040
Surely you miss him dearly.

169
00:13:19,920 --> 00:13:23,720
Now that we have come, let us pour water
to dedicate merit to his spirit.

170
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,320
Yes.

171
00:13:53,600 --> 00:13:56,600
Pour water to dedicate merit
to the departed kinfolks.

172
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,520
Do you know how to proceed,

173
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,440
or has that too vanished
from your recollection?

174
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:44,520
<i>Why am I</i>

175
00:15:45,560 --> 00:15:46,760
<i>actually sad?</i>

176
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:49,920
<i>Klao's father isn't even mine.</i>

177
00:15:51,680 --> 00:15:52,880
Dear me…

178
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:56,680
Has the ritual offered no comfort
to your troubled spirit?

179
00:15:57,920 --> 00:15:59,840
It pains me greatly to see you thus.

180
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:07,000
Auntie…

181
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:09,880
My Lady,

182
00:16:11,120 --> 00:16:12,320
I am…

183
00:16:12,400 --> 00:16:13,800
profoundly grateful to you.

184
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,240
Dear Klao,

185
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,200
spare me the formalities.

186
00:16:21,320 --> 00:16:23,000
Surely you have forgotten that

187
00:16:23,600 --> 00:16:25,760
your mother died
when you were still so young.

188
00:16:25,840 --> 00:16:28,600
In days past,
you would follow me wherever I went.

189
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:32,040
It is true.

190
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:34,880
It was her you sought so dearly,

191
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:38,280
I fear you meant to claim her as your own.

192
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,680
Do address me as "Aunt,"
as you did before.

193
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,280
Aunt.

194
00:16:53,800 --> 00:16:54,800
My father…

195
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:59,680
Did he really commit a wrongdoing
and get executed?

196
00:17:07,280 --> 00:17:08,800
Stop!

197
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:11,319
I beg of you! Please!

198
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,839
I offer but a glimpse of the truth.

199
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,440
Who makes such a stir there?

200
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:17,720
At the outskirts of the temple,

201
00:17:17,800 --> 00:17:20,480
it could only be that strange oracle,
my Lady.

202
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:22,160
Phop,

203
00:17:22,240 --> 00:17:23,480
grant them your aid.

204
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,760
-Of course.
-You wretched oracle!

205
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:27,880
You stir discord between husband and wife.

206
00:17:31,720 --> 00:17:32,600
Chuay.

207
00:17:32,680 --> 00:17:34,880
See to it that Klao
and my mother remain here.

208
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,560
Dear Klao.

209
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:52,800
You vile, wicked wretch!
How dare you speak thus?

210
00:17:53,400 --> 00:17:56,480
If there is truly no other,
why this unrest?

211
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,160
This lady speaks the truth.

212
00:17:58,240 --> 00:18:00,600
If your heart
be free of such lustful desires,

213
00:18:00,680 --> 00:18:03,040
why this sudden ferocious outburst?

214
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:05,080
-Curse you!
-You!

215
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,800
What manner of business is this?

216
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,920
This wretched oracle has gone mad,

217
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,480
for the prophecy delivered
is unsound and senseless,

218
00:18:17,560 --> 00:18:20,080
turning my wife against me.

219
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:22,080
It is whispered in every corner.

220
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:24,000
I am entirely innocent, my Lord.

221
00:18:24,600 --> 00:18:27,520
I did but give voice to the prophecy.

222
00:18:31,960 --> 00:18:32,840
You are Dear Klao?

223
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:35,720
You son of a rogue!

224
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:37,200
Return with another outburst?

225
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:39,640
-It is he.
-You son of a rogue.

226
00:18:39,720 --> 00:18:41,120
What is your business here?

227
00:18:41,200 --> 00:18:43,320
-Why here? Another outburst?
-Indeed.

228
00:18:43,400 --> 00:18:46,720
-You son of a rogue.
-Wretch.

229
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,280
Return to your wretched dwelling.

230
00:18:50,360 --> 00:18:53,040
Go away! Return at once!

231
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:54,280
You witless!

232
00:18:56,880 --> 00:18:57,960
Klao.

233
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:00,560
Young man…

234
00:19:00,640 --> 00:19:01,720
What troubles you so?

235
00:19:10,040 --> 00:19:10,880
Fortune teller!

236
00:19:15,520 --> 00:19:16,880
It really is you.

237
00:19:18,160 --> 00:19:19,400
Recognize me and the hair?

238
00:19:19,960 --> 00:19:21,080
Hair?

239
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:23,840
My hair is as pristine as ever.

240
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:26,360
No, that's not what I meant.

241
00:19:26,440 --> 00:19:28,040
It's me, Nakun,

242
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,480
the guy who visited your pavilion
a few days ago.

243
00:19:30,560 --> 00:19:31,720
Pavilion?

244
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,000
Indeed.

245
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:40,880
Once, I nearly became an oracle,

246
00:19:42,280 --> 00:19:44,840
serving the king at his pavilion.

247
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,320
Cease this, Oracle.

248
00:19:49,400 --> 00:19:50,680
Stop this at once, Klao.

249
00:19:50,760 --> 00:19:52,480
You have caused a great disturbance.

250
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:57,320
I am a lady,
though born in a man's guise.

251
00:19:58,080 --> 00:20:01,040
Thereafter, I was shunned and ill-treated.

252
00:20:01,720 --> 00:20:04,080
My dream has crumbled to dust.

253
00:20:05,520 --> 00:20:06,800
Stay out of this for now.

254
00:20:06,880 --> 00:20:08,280
Let me talk to her.

255
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:12,080
Please stop playing around.
It's me, Nakun…

256
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:21,120
Wrong place, wrong time,
and wrong circumstances.

257
00:20:21,960 --> 00:20:25,000
The promise and the wish

258
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:29,080
shall restore what was lost
and set wrongs aright!

259
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:49,440
Young man.

260
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:52,640
Are you hungry?

261
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:02,240
You know that
I traveled through time, don't you?

262
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:03,680
Klao, enough!

263
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:05,400
Return to the manor.

264
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:07,280
Oracle, you should leave now.

265
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:08,240
Hey!

266
00:21:09,440 --> 00:21:10,520
Don't leave just yet.

267
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:12,840
Let me talk to her, please.

268
00:21:12,920 --> 00:21:14,200
Cease this at once, Klao.

269
00:21:20,560 --> 00:21:22,240
Pray, help us!

270
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:24,960
Giants have descended
upon the kingdom!

271
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:27,640
I, Sida, must now take my leave.

272
00:21:37,720 --> 00:21:38,760
Hey!

273
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:41,160
I take the form of a golden deer

274
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:44,320
-and vanish into the wind.
-Oracle! Halt at once!

275
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:45,280
Oracle!

276
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:46,720
-I'm gone!
-Don't go!

277
00:21:46,800 --> 00:21:48,600
-Hey!
-Klao!

278
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,200
Is my meaning lost?
Return to the manor!

279
00:21:53,280 --> 00:21:54,480
I'm not heading back!

280
00:21:55,040 --> 00:21:57,000
I told you I wanted to talk to her first!

281
00:21:57,080 --> 00:22:00,000
Speaking with her
only draws you nearer to madness.

282
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:01,160
Come with me.

283
00:22:04,640 --> 00:22:05,520
Let me go!

284
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:08,040
I shall let you go,

285
00:22:08,120 --> 00:22:10,760
if you vow not to leave me.

286
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:14,000
God!

287
00:22:14,080 --> 00:22:14,920
Hey!

288
00:22:18,040 --> 00:22:20,360
Can you not be this much of a nuisance?

289
00:22:20,440 --> 00:22:21,920
I know you're worried about me.

290
00:22:22,720 --> 00:22:24,200
I know we're childhood friends,

291
00:22:24,280 --> 00:22:26,080
but we're grown-ups now.

292
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:27,640
I can go wherever I want.

293
00:22:28,720 --> 00:22:29,920
If we're really friends

294
00:22:30,440 --> 00:22:31,520
and you care about me,

295
00:22:32,440 --> 00:22:33,640
give me a say in this.

296
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:36,360
My actions are for your sake.

297
00:22:38,280 --> 00:22:40,360
You ought not wander off
of your own accord,

298
00:22:42,520 --> 00:22:44,920
for some ill-intentioned soul
seeks to do you harm.

299
00:22:46,560 --> 00:22:48,040
Do me harm?

300
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:55,880
It is you who is harming me.

301
00:23:02,480 --> 00:23:03,440
Forgive me.

302
00:23:06,440 --> 00:23:09,120
If caring means
watching over me like I'm a convict,

303
00:23:10,400 --> 00:23:11,600
then you'd better stop.

304
00:23:12,400 --> 00:23:13,320
It's uncomfortable.

305
00:23:40,440 --> 00:23:42,440
May I speak with you at last?

306
00:23:45,800 --> 00:23:48,280
You have kept a silence
the entire way back.

307
00:23:48,360 --> 00:23:49,640
I won't talk.

308
00:23:50,160 --> 00:23:51,720
No one should disturb me either.

309
00:23:53,680 --> 00:23:55,120
Master Klao! Master!

310
00:23:56,800 --> 00:23:57,840
Master Klao.

311
00:24:02,680 --> 00:24:03,560
Phop.

312
00:24:05,760 --> 00:24:07,840
Perhaps you have been
unduly harsh with him.

313
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:09,720
My concern was for his well-being.

314
00:24:11,560 --> 00:24:13,720
I thought the temple
would afford him solace,

315
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:16,160
yet the presence of the masses

316
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:19,080
has only deepened his derangement.

317
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:22,600
Despite my many concerns for you,

318
00:24:23,560 --> 00:24:27,600
I have never constrained you.
Or have I been mistaken?

319
00:24:32,600 --> 00:24:34,960
The more you care and love,

320
00:24:35,040 --> 00:24:36,640
the kinder you must be.

321
00:24:37,280 --> 00:24:40,840
You cannot simply force him
against his will.

322
00:24:59,520 --> 00:25:00,880
<i>One moment he's sweet,</i>

323
00:25:00,960 --> 00:25:02,240
<i>then he's fierce as a dog.</i>

324
00:25:02,320 --> 00:25:04,000
<i>He's got multiple personalities?</i>

325
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,160
<i>No.</i>

326
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:08,240
<i>He's only got one personality</i>

327
00:25:08,800 --> 00:25:10,760
<i>and that is being way too nosy about me!</i>

328
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:17,120
<i>I want to go home already.</i>

329
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:18,680
<i>If there are no meteor showers,</i>

330
00:25:18,760 --> 00:25:20,760
<i>then what am I supposed to do?</i>

331
00:25:24,200 --> 00:25:25,280
Wrong time…

332
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:26,400
Wrong place…

333
00:25:26,480 --> 00:25:27,480
Wrong circumstances…

334
00:25:28,640 --> 00:25:29,680
<i>Wrong time</i>

335
00:25:30,240 --> 00:25:31,320
<i>and wrong place.</i>

336
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:36,000
<i>She must've known</i>
<i>I traveled through time.</i>

337
00:25:37,600 --> 00:25:38,960
The promise

338
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:40,640
and the wish

339
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:41,800
shall restore

340
00:25:41,880 --> 00:25:44,800
what was lost and set wrongs aright.

341
00:25:46,400 --> 00:25:48,280
What promise did you make, and to whom?

342
00:25:48,360 --> 00:25:50,960
Someone from the past
awaits its fulfillment.

343
00:25:52,240 --> 00:25:54,200
<i>What promise did Klao make, and to whom?</i>

344
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:56,240
<i>What did he fail to fulfill?</i>

345
00:25:57,040 --> 00:25:59,800
<i>Why didn't the fortune teller</i>
<i>make things easier for me?</i>

346
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:09,200
<i>Did the professor</i>
<i>teach me anything about this?</i>

347
00:26:21,280 --> 00:26:24,800
Just ask the student
who's sleeping…

348
00:26:24,880 --> 00:26:29,200
has he just traveled through time…

349
00:26:29,280 --> 00:26:32,720
and met what or whom?

350
00:26:34,080 --> 00:26:36,600
<i>Gosh! Why did you fall asleep, Nakun?</i>

351
00:26:37,360 --> 00:26:39,280
<i>What else did she say?</i>

352
00:26:43,840 --> 00:26:46,600
Is it to be able to adapt to
the settings of that era?

353
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:48,400
You're actually correct,

354
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,280
but not entirely.

355
00:26:51,280 --> 00:26:53,080
Ideally,

356
00:26:53,160 --> 00:26:55,240
we should give the main character

357
00:26:55,320 --> 00:26:57,960
a mission or goal.

358
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:02,200
What?

359
00:27:02,280 --> 00:27:04,680
If you could go back in time,

360
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:06,280
what would your mission be?

361
00:27:09,280 --> 00:27:10,240
I don't know.

362
00:27:11,200 --> 00:27:12,040
It might be…

363
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:13,880
to get plenty of sleep

364
00:27:14,720 --> 00:27:16,320
without being disturbed by you.

365
00:27:17,000 --> 00:27:18,920
You look pretty worn out.

366
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:23,160
Wanna go to Gangnam Clinic after class

367
00:27:23,240 --> 00:27:24,840
and get some vitamins?

368
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:26,040
Sounds nice.

369
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:28,320
But can you let me doze off first?

370
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:29,880
<i>Stop talking to Thee.</i>

371
00:27:29,960 --> 00:27:32,120
<i>What did the professor say again?</i>

372
00:27:35,160 --> 00:27:36,920
Ideally,

373
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:39,160
we should give the main character

374
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:41,840
a mission or goal.

375
00:27:42,520 --> 00:27:43,360
For example,

376
00:27:44,400 --> 00:27:46,200
the main character

377
00:27:46,280 --> 00:27:49,880
could travel back in time
to alter history,

378
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:55,160
or solve a cold case in the past

379
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:59,040
that then provides the key
to their investigation in the present.

380
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:01,600
Or the main character

381
00:28:02,160 --> 00:28:05,880
could travel back in time
to fall in love with someone

382
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:09,520
they would never meet in the present.

383
00:28:09,600 --> 00:28:12,840
<i>For the most part,</i>
<i>after accomplishing their mission,</i>

384
00:28:12,920 --> 00:28:14,560
<i>they'll learn and understand,</i>

385
00:28:14,640 --> 00:28:16,720
<i>which leads to character development.</i>

386
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:17,960
At that moment,

387
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,520
the goal of time travel

388
00:28:22,920 --> 00:28:24,000
will be achieved.

389
00:28:24,720 --> 00:28:26,840
Will the character return to the present?

390
00:28:28,360 --> 00:28:30,320
What an excellent question.

391
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:31,240
Yes.

392
00:28:31,800 --> 00:28:34,480
It could be through a mirror,

393
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:36,680
by drowning,

394
00:28:37,880 --> 00:28:40,760
or via a traditional Thai costume.

395
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:42,760
However…

396
00:28:44,080 --> 00:28:48,160
should the main character
fail their mission,

397
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:52,280
the portal will be closed forever,

398
00:28:52,360 --> 00:28:55,760
preventing their return to their world.

399
00:28:59,520 --> 00:29:00,440
My mission!

400
00:29:14,320 --> 00:29:15,280
Chuay.

401
00:29:16,800 --> 00:29:17,640
Gosh.

402
00:29:18,280 --> 00:29:19,520
I'm sorry, Chuay.

403
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:21,920
Think nothing of it, Master.

404
00:29:24,840 --> 00:29:27,720
Has your displeasure with Lord Phop
now come to an end?

405
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:29,960
Chuay, do you have

406
00:29:30,720 --> 00:29:32,400
a pencil or a pen?

407
00:29:33,680 --> 00:29:34,720
A pencil, Master?

408
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:38,240
Do you want it for applying to the face?

409
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:40,920
No, not marl.

410
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:43,640
A pen or a pencil, you know?

411
00:29:43,720 --> 00:29:44,720
A pen-seal, Master?

412
00:29:46,320 --> 00:29:47,560
Oh, Master.

413
00:29:47,640 --> 00:29:48,800
Where am I to seek one?

414
00:29:48,880 --> 00:29:51,320
Might a duck or chicken pen
suffice in its stead?

415
00:29:57,160 --> 00:29:58,400
Go and get me one,

416
00:29:58,480 --> 00:30:00,160
or your lips will bleed.

417
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:09,040
I'm telling you,
it's what's used for writing.

418
00:30:09,120 --> 00:30:12,480
It looks just like an ordinary pen,
like a quill with ink.

419
00:30:12,560 --> 00:30:14,400
A bird that cries "ka-ka-ka"?

420
00:30:14,480 --> 00:30:15,480
Yeah.

421
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:18,080
-That kind.
-"Ka-ka-ka-ka"?

422
00:30:18,160 --> 00:30:19,000
Right?

423
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:22,200
What is it used for?

424
00:30:22,280 --> 00:30:24,520
I told you it's for writing!

425
00:30:24,600 --> 00:30:25,800
Writing, Master?

426
00:30:25,880 --> 00:30:27,400
Writing!

427
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:29,000
-In this manner?
-Yeah.

428
00:30:45,400 --> 00:30:46,280
Here, Master.

429
00:30:56,600 --> 00:30:59,320
Chuay is unversed
in the use of scholarly instruments,

430
00:30:59,400 --> 00:31:01,480
just speak to me, and I shall supply it.

431
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:08,560
How does it work?

432
00:31:08,640 --> 00:31:10,320
Can you show me how it works?

433
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:16,480
You can write, yet these instruments
are unfamiliar to you?

434
00:31:16,560 --> 00:31:18,080
Do comply with his wishes.

435
00:31:18,160 --> 00:31:20,200
It is not ours to meddle in such matters.

436
00:31:25,360 --> 00:31:27,120
Behold, Master Klao.

437
00:31:27,960 --> 00:31:29,440
Thus is it used.

438
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:31,160
Do try it, Master.

439
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:34,160
Back when…

440
00:31:37,360 --> 00:31:38,440
I mean, in Phichit,

441
00:31:38,960 --> 00:31:40,600
pens commonly used there

442
00:31:40,680 --> 00:31:42,000
come pre-filled with ink.

443
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:46,320
It slowly comes out from the tip.

444
00:31:46,400 --> 00:31:47,760
No need to refill the ink.

445
00:31:53,480 --> 00:31:56,600
I wish to accompany you to Phichit
and behold its splendor

446
00:31:56,680 --> 00:31:59,120
Very well. Depart this place at once,

447
00:31:59,200 --> 00:32:00,200
and return not.

448
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:03,160
Take your leave.

449
00:32:03,240 --> 00:32:05,160
-You must leave.
-No, it's you.

450
00:32:05,240 --> 00:32:07,360
-No, it's you.
-Go fight outside.

451
00:32:07,440 --> 00:32:08,960
I can't focus.

452
00:32:09,920 --> 00:32:11,600
Also, shut the door.

453
00:32:11,680 --> 00:32:12,920
The fault is yours.

454
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,000
Yes, Master.

455
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:19,160
Begone, if you wish.

456
00:32:19,240 --> 00:32:20,800
Your master drove us off.

457
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:22,680
Since when have you become my master?

458
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:42,160
<i>My mission: Find out whatever happened</i>
<i>to the real Klao.</i>

459
00:32:53,440 --> 00:32:55,720
I told you not to come in yet, Chuay.

460
00:33:05,800 --> 00:33:09,120
Word from the kitchens
says you've been here all day,

461
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:10,920
neglecting even your meals.

462
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:14,760
Well…

463
00:33:14,840 --> 00:33:17,840
I just want to finish my writing first.

464
00:33:17,920 --> 00:33:20,720
I am pleased that
you have resumed your scholarly pursuits,

465
00:33:20,800 --> 00:33:23,160
which is far preferable to indulgence.

466
00:33:24,120 --> 00:33:26,880
-If you're forcing me to have dinner--
-No.

467
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:34,280
I shall not oppose your wish to remain.

468
00:33:36,840 --> 00:33:38,800
I have brought this for you.

469
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:43,920
Take some nourishment
before your stomach complains.

470
00:33:46,480 --> 00:33:48,360
It is of the finest quality,

471
00:33:50,680 --> 00:33:52,760
brought by traders from across China.

472
00:33:53,720 --> 00:33:56,080
Oranges are just 40 baht a kilo
in Bangkok.

473
00:33:56,880 --> 00:33:58,880
What was that you said?

474
00:34:00,880 --> 00:34:03,120
Just leave the basket here. I…

475
00:34:03,200 --> 00:34:04,520
I'll have them myself.

476
00:34:14,639 --> 00:34:16,760
Your hands are stained with ink.

477
00:34:17,719 --> 00:34:19,639
I shall prepare them for you.

478
00:34:23,400 --> 00:34:25,639
Why are the candles
yet unlit at this hour?

479
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:29,600
Your eyes might ache.

480
00:35:33,920 --> 00:35:35,080
Thanks.

481
00:35:37,440 --> 00:35:39,240
Forgive me for this morning.

482
00:35:43,040 --> 00:35:45,280
The fault was entirely mine
for pushing you.

483
00:35:47,240 --> 00:35:48,600
Do not hold it against me.

484
00:35:53,840 --> 00:35:55,760
I'd like to apologize as well.

485
00:35:56,840 --> 00:35:58,800
I was being rude to you.

486
00:36:01,480 --> 00:36:02,560
Why did you laugh?

487
00:36:04,720 --> 00:36:06,600
A slight stain of ink mars your face,

488
00:36:06,680 --> 00:36:09,320
like that of an aged and dirty feline.

489
00:36:12,560 --> 00:36:13,600
Here.

490
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:15,400
I shall wipe it away.

491
00:36:18,080 --> 00:36:19,480
Well…

492
00:37:27,160 --> 00:37:28,000
Kong.

493
00:37:28,080 --> 00:37:30,600
Why do you breathe upon me, you bovine?

494
00:37:30,680 --> 00:37:33,040
It was you who turned towards me,

495
00:37:33,120 --> 00:37:34,640
you imbecile.

496
00:37:34,720 --> 00:37:36,560
Chuay! Kong!

497
00:37:39,800 --> 00:37:42,680
I entrusted him to your care,

498
00:37:43,280 --> 00:37:45,200
and yet you indulge in petty squabbles.

499
00:37:46,360 --> 00:37:49,400
Do you wish to be caned upon your back?

500
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:51,960
No, my Lord.

501
00:37:52,040 --> 00:37:53,680
It shall not occur again, my Lord.

502
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:38,880
I…

503
00:38:41,280 --> 00:38:42,520
shall take my leave now,

504
00:38:44,240 --> 00:38:47,080
that you may write with a clear mind.

505
00:38:47,800 --> 00:38:49,680
All right.

506
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:51,920
Yes, my Lord.

507
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:58,160
Tarry not too long into the night?

508
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:39,760
Perform such a massage
with your own hands,

509
00:39:39,840 --> 00:39:41,760
or have your servant assist you.

510
00:39:42,560 --> 00:39:44,200
It will give you peaceful sleep.

511
00:39:47,920 --> 00:39:48,800
Kaew.

512
00:39:48,880 --> 00:39:50,920
Continue to massage him after me.

513
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,000
Certainly.

514
00:39:59,520 --> 00:40:01,560
Avoid those of unsettled minds,

515
00:40:01,640 --> 00:40:03,480
for whatever they utter,

516
00:40:03,560 --> 00:40:05,200
Klao is apt to take as truth,

517
00:40:06,560 --> 00:40:08,400
and his condition shall only worsen,

518
00:40:08,480 --> 00:40:10,200
as though he were cursed.

519
00:40:12,960 --> 00:40:14,480
I see it the same way.

520
00:40:17,160 --> 00:40:19,440
But do not confine him
within the manor.

521
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:22,320
Even convicts in a prison
descend into madness,

522
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:25,600
for they dwell only in shadows.

523
00:40:28,200 --> 00:40:30,120
To be concerned for his sake,

524
00:40:30,200 --> 00:40:32,280
one must do so with a measured heart.

525
00:40:34,160 --> 00:40:35,400
So nice…

526
00:40:35,480 --> 00:40:39,080
This feels like the spa
I visited in Ekkamai.

527
00:40:40,560 --> 00:40:41,960
What did you say?

528
00:40:42,840 --> 00:40:44,480
Oh, forget I said anything.

529
00:40:49,960 --> 00:40:53,360
Do you truly believe his present condition
arises from indulgence alone?

530
00:40:54,560 --> 00:40:57,800
If so, he should've returned
to his former self by now.

531
00:40:57,880 --> 00:40:59,520
I fear there is something deeper.

532
00:41:01,400 --> 00:41:02,760
Opium?

533
00:41:05,040 --> 00:41:06,480
I find it inconclusive.

534
00:41:08,640 --> 00:41:09,560
Now, tell me,

535
00:41:09,640 --> 00:41:12,920
have you discovered his whereabouts
during his absence?

536
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:19,120
It seems not yet.

537
00:41:21,680 --> 00:41:23,760
To unveil his whereabouts

538
00:41:23,840 --> 00:41:26,280
shall enable us
to better discern his condition.

539
00:41:30,960 --> 00:41:33,360
This truly warms my heart, Klao.

540
00:41:34,560 --> 00:41:36,960
You speak with far greater reason.

541
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:41,360
Well…

542
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:44,960
It's probably due to the temple's grace

543
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:47,560
and the merits I made for my father.

544
00:41:47,640 --> 00:41:49,200
That's why I feel a bit better.

545
00:41:49,280 --> 00:41:51,400
Your memories of your father returned?

546
00:42:02,880 --> 00:42:03,880
Yes…

547
00:42:04,600 --> 00:42:05,920
I…

548
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,960
I saw him at the court in my dream.

549
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:17,400
It is known as the Court of Assessors.

550
00:42:18,840 --> 00:42:19,760
How wonderful.

551
00:42:19,840 --> 00:42:21,800
Do you recall your father?

552
00:42:25,440 --> 00:42:26,880
It is owing to Jom's practice.

553
00:42:26,960 --> 00:42:28,520
I must hasten the massage.

554
00:42:28,600 --> 00:42:30,600
-Ow, ow.
-It is unnecessary.

555
00:42:33,320 --> 00:42:35,920
Only standard practice.
Let not your wit run ahead.

556
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,560
In my dream,

557
00:42:44,760 --> 00:42:46,920
I saw my father

558
00:42:48,280 --> 00:42:51,400
being sentenced to be slashed with a spear

559
00:42:53,800 --> 00:42:54,680
for…

560
00:42:57,120 --> 00:42:58,040
his part…

561
00:42:59,240 --> 00:43:01,080
in corruption

562
00:43:01,160 --> 00:43:02,040
and bribery.

563
00:43:02,120 --> 00:43:04,280
With a spear?

564
00:43:11,640 --> 00:43:13,720
I heard it from the man,

565
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:15,960
whom I took for their leader,

566
00:43:18,480 --> 00:43:20,480
order his back slashed with a spear.

567
00:43:21,520 --> 00:43:24,000
What he meant
was a lashing to his back.

568
00:43:29,680 --> 00:43:30,880
Lashing…

569
00:43:34,440 --> 00:43:35,400
with…

570
00:43:37,280 --> 00:43:38,600
a rattan cane.

571
00:43:40,720 --> 00:43:43,200
But my father was innocent!

572
00:43:44,960 --> 00:43:47,240
I do believe your words.

573
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:51,280
Lord Preechapiban is guiltless.

574
00:43:51,840 --> 00:43:53,280
The common folk

575
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,960
remained in accord
with the jury's verdict.

576
00:43:57,720 --> 00:43:59,720
Since your return to the capital,

577
00:43:59,800 --> 00:44:02,040
you have each night drifted

578
00:44:02,120 --> 00:44:04,120
toward indulgence in the market's corners.

579
00:44:05,480 --> 00:44:07,920
The sorrow you bear
must be beyond measure.

580
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:13,920
I see now,

581
00:44:14,640 --> 00:44:15,880
from what I was told,

582
00:44:17,720 --> 00:44:19,800
some matters
are best left in the shadows.

583
00:44:25,920 --> 00:44:28,040
What a pitiable soul he is,

584
00:44:29,440 --> 00:44:32,080
having lost all memory of himself.

585
00:44:35,640 --> 00:44:37,040
Jom.

586
00:44:37,120 --> 00:44:40,440
What would you do
were I to lose all recollection of you?

587
00:44:42,080 --> 00:44:44,040
Nothing would need to be done.

588
00:44:47,080 --> 00:44:48,720
Utterly heartless.

589
00:44:50,160 --> 00:44:51,960
Nothing would need to be done,

590
00:44:52,840 --> 00:44:54,720
for my care would endure,

591
00:44:55,400 --> 00:44:57,440
even should you know me not.

592
00:45:10,400 --> 00:45:11,720
Jom…

593
00:45:12,800 --> 00:45:14,600
I am a physician.

594
00:45:14,680 --> 00:45:17,280
It is my duty to tend all who suffer,

595
00:45:18,960 --> 00:45:20,280
and you are no exception.

596
00:45:31,840 --> 00:45:34,560
Do you hold me in affection,

597
00:45:35,320 --> 00:45:37,160
or do you despise me,

598
00:45:37,920 --> 00:45:39,120
Jom?

599
00:45:52,520 --> 00:45:55,600
<i>He brought up drinking</i>
<i>at the market again.</i>

600
00:45:55,680 --> 00:45:59,440
<i>Is this why this deadpan-looking guy</i>
<i>doesn't like me visiting the market?</i>

601
00:45:59,520 --> 00:46:00,440
Klao.

602
00:46:02,400 --> 00:46:06,400
Your father's affair has been settled.
Let it remain in the past.

603
00:46:06,480 --> 00:46:08,080
Cease your concern.

604
00:46:14,440 --> 00:46:15,960
Good heavens!

605
00:46:16,040 --> 00:46:18,960
Masters…

606
00:46:20,080 --> 00:46:23,880
A wallago of such remarkable size
was secured this day.

607
00:46:23,960 --> 00:46:26,360
Will you not take a taste?

608
00:46:28,440 --> 00:46:29,960
Oh, deary me!

609
00:46:31,280 --> 00:46:33,760
Spicy flavors
are not to Master Klao's taste,

610
00:46:33,840 --> 00:46:36,520
yet this contains no such heat.

611
00:46:40,920 --> 00:46:45,120
My dishes are of unique flavor,

612
00:46:45,200 --> 00:46:47,920
for I cook by no recipe.

613
00:47:10,440 --> 00:47:12,000
It is most true.

614
00:47:14,360 --> 00:47:15,920
Though the dishes lack heat,

615
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:17,920
the excellence of their flavor endures.

616
00:47:23,280 --> 00:47:26,640
You flatter me far too much, Master.

617
00:47:39,640 --> 00:47:40,840
So clingy.

618
00:47:42,400 --> 00:47:43,240
Deary me.

619
00:47:43,320 --> 00:47:46,400
Were I to serve you
spicy ant-larvae salad,

620
00:47:46,480 --> 00:47:49,520
you would rejoice
as though rich fortunes were yours.

621
00:47:51,440 --> 00:47:53,520
As for that dish,

622
00:47:54,240 --> 00:47:56,320
I shall decline, if it pleases you.

623
00:48:01,080 --> 00:48:02,160
So…

624
00:48:02,240 --> 00:48:04,240
Sorn, my beloved,

625
00:48:04,320 --> 00:48:07,840
once secured
a colossal weaver-ant nest with larvae.

626
00:48:07,920 --> 00:48:10,560
I prepared the spicy ant-larvae salad
for my master,

627
00:48:10,640 --> 00:48:12,600
pouring all my heart into it,

628
00:48:12,680 --> 00:48:15,120
rushing about in haste,

629
00:48:15,200 --> 00:48:18,640
indulging in herbal spirits,

630
00:48:18,720 --> 00:48:20,880
and tending the child within me.

631
00:48:23,880 --> 00:48:25,240
So…

632
00:48:26,160 --> 00:48:29,000
-it didn't turn out well?
-Absolutely flavorful!

633
00:48:29,080 --> 00:48:30,280
It was astonishing!

634
00:48:30,360 --> 00:48:33,440
One serving
could not possibly suffice to sate him.

635
00:48:36,440 --> 00:48:38,240
Then, my lips were bitten.

636
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:39,560
Bitten?

637
00:48:40,760 --> 00:48:43,320
Can ant larvae even bite?

638
00:48:43,920 --> 00:48:45,560
Upon closer inspection,

639
00:48:45,640 --> 00:48:48,120
it seemed
I had been feasting upon termites.

640
00:49:00,520 --> 00:49:04,280
My lady scolded me with such fury
that one of us collapsed.

641
00:49:05,000 --> 00:49:06,600
Though it was she,

642
00:49:06,680 --> 00:49:09,320
for she had been reproaching me
for countless hours.

643
00:49:09,400 --> 00:49:14,360
Moreover, I was compelled
to dispose of the herbal spirits,

644
00:49:14,440 --> 00:49:16,680
and she banished Sorn from the manor.

645
00:49:17,360 --> 00:49:18,720
You were guilty,

646
00:49:18,800 --> 00:49:21,160
so why was it Sorn

647
00:49:21,240 --> 00:49:22,840
who got punished instead?

648
00:49:22,920 --> 00:49:24,640
I always go by one belief.

649
00:49:24,720 --> 00:49:28,560
To shift all blame I incur onto others.

650
00:49:28,640 --> 00:49:30,800
It is far more comforting so.

651
00:49:43,280 --> 00:49:46,480
Master laughed with great joy.

652
00:49:46,560 --> 00:49:49,600
Would you care to partake
of the wallago curry,

653
00:49:49,680 --> 00:49:53,240
or the spicy ant-larvae salad
with termites?

654
00:50:19,080 --> 00:50:19,960
Tasty!

655
00:50:38,280 --> 00:50:39,640
What a delight.

656
00:50:39,720 --> 00:50:42,480
It's been so long
since I last saw your radiant smile.

657
00:50:42,560 --> 00:50:47,400
Well, a lot of things
have been keeping me from smiling.

658
00:50:47,480 --> 00:50:48,600
That said,

659
00:50:48,680 --> 00:50:51,360
it seems I must summon her
to converse with you each day.

660
00:50:51,440 --> 00:50:53,480
She's so much fun to talk to.

661
00:51:02,520 --> 00:51:03,680
Tomorrow…

662
00:51:04,360 --> 00:51:06,040
can I go to…

663
00:51:06,120 --> 00:51:08,560
the market with Muan?

664
00:51:08,640 --> 00:51:09,840
Like…

665
00:51:09,920 --> 00:51:11,680
Maybe it'll put me in a better mood

666
00:51:11,760 --> 00:51:14,600
and bring back some memories.

667
00:51:19,960 --> 00:51:21,560
I would grant it,

668
00:51:22,520 --> 00:51:24,080
were it not so dangerous there.

669
00:51:24,160 --> 00:51:25,440
Dangerous again?

670
00:51:26,680 --> 00:51:28,240
What's the deal with the market?

671
00:51:28,320 --> 00:51:30,560
Why keep telling me it's dangerous there?

672
00:51:33,880 --> 00:51:36,000
It's okay if you can't answer me.

673
00:51:36,080 --> 00:51:38,040
If it's that dangerous,

674
00:51:38,120 --> 00:51:39,800
go with me.

675
00:51:39,880 --> 00:51:41,600
This way, you can protect me.

676
00:51:49,480 --> 00:51:50,960
Please.

677
00:51:55,040 --> 00:51:56,800
Please, my Phop.

678
00:51:57,960 --> 00:51:59,240
Please…

679
00:52:00,240 --> 00:52:01,320
You…

680
00:52:02,640 --> 00:52:04,360
What title did you just address me?

681
00:52:04,440 --> 00:52:05,720
My Phop.

682
00:52:06,360 --> 00:52:09,000
Please, take me there, my Phop.

683
00:52:16,040 --> 00:52:17,440
Were I not bound to patrol,

684
00:52:18,440 --> 00:52:19,960
I would take you there.

685
00:52:20,040 --> 00:52:20,920
Yes!

686
00:52:21,000 --> 00:52:24,880
You promised! Thank you!

687
00:52:37,920 --> 00:52:39,760
Thank you so much.

688
00:53:16,040 --> 00:53:17,120
<i>Move!</i>

689
00:53:17,680 --> 00:53:19,120
<i>Forward!</i>

690
00:53:19,200 --> 00:53:20,240
Move!

691
00:53:34,600 --> 00:53:36,400
Lord Preechapiban.

692
00:53:36,960 --> 00:53:39,600
Will you confess to your misdeeds?

693
00:53:40,640 --> 00:53:42,760
Your punishment shall be mitigated,

694
00:53:42,840 --> 00:53:44,800
lightened to mere captivity.

695
00:53:49,880 --> 00:53:50,760
No.

696
00:53:52,480 --> 00:53:54,040
I did not commit the misdeeds.

697
00:53:55,280 --> 00:53:57,320
Why then must I confess?

698
00:54:00,840 --> 00:54:01,880
Two rounds

699
00:54:02,640 --> 00:54:03,960
of the lash.

700
00:54:06,800 --> 00:54:07,840
Father!

701
00:54:10,080 --> 00:54:11,200
Klao!

702
00:54:23,360 --> 00:54:24,200
Father!

703
00:54:36,440 --> 00:54:37,840
<i>Klao's father was innocent,</i>

704
00:54:37,920 --> 00:54:39,560
<i>but he still got punished.</i>

705
00:54:41,120 --> 00:54:41,960
<i>Klao.</i>

706
00:54:42,480 --> 00:54:45,440
<i>Your heart was so broken</i>
<i>that you went drinking at the market.</i>

707
00:54:45,520 --> 00:54:47,120
<i>Or…</i>

708
00:54:47,200 --> 00:54:49,120
<i>is there something else to this?</i>

709
00:55:05,640 --> 00:55:07,080
Sai.

710
00:55:07,160 --> 00:55:09,400
Do you take pleasure in feeding the fish?

711
00:55:09,480 --> 00:55:11,440
I take more pleasure in feeding you.

712
00:55:13,520 --> 00:55:15,600
-You do never cease to amaze me.
-Chuay.

713
00:55:16,240 --> 00:55:17,080
Yes, Master?

714
00:55:17,160 --> 00:55:18,240
Where is Phop?

715
00:55:18,320 --> 00:55:21,160
The Lord was summoned to his post at dawn.

716
00:55:22,720 --> 00:55:26,840
<i>When I stay home doing nothing,</i>
<i>he does nothing but watch over me.</i>

717
00:55:26,920 --> 00:55:30,000
<i>And he went on duty</i>
<i>the moment we made our promise.</i>

718
00:55:31,280 --> 00:55:33,880
Is there a matter
you wish to discuss with him?

719
00:55:33,960 --> 00:55:34,800
No, there isn't.

720
00:55:35,680 --> 00:55:37,440
I just want to visit the capital.

721
00:55:37,520 --> 00:55:40,320
Have you sought his permission, Master?

722
00:55:43,120 --> 00:55:43,960
Yes.

723
00:55:44,480 --> 00:55:46,760
I discussed it with him last night.

724
00:55:49,040 --> 00:55:50,240
He's letting me go there.

725
00:55:53,920 --> 00:55:57,400
Might I suggest that
you remain here until he returns, Master?

726
00:55:59,160 --> 00:56:02,040
It'll already be too late
by the time he returns.

727
00:56:02,120 --> 00:56:05,320
If so, you should go there tomorrow.

728
00:56:06,080 --> 00:56:07,000
Chuay.

729
00:56:09,800 --> 00:56:11,720
I'm so lonely I could die here.

730
00:56:12,760 --> 00:56:14,240
I've been staying in the manor,

731
00:56:14,320 --> 00:56:15,720
cut off from the light of day

732
00:56:15,800 --> 00:56:17,400
and from life itself.

733
00:56:18,680 --> 00:56:20,560
Why don't you feel sorry for me, Chuay?

734
00:56:20,640 --> 00:56:22,760
Didn't you say

735
00:56:23,320 --> 00:56:24,600
you loved me

736
00:56:25,840 --> 00:56:27,680
and were loyal to me?

737
00:56:40,440 --> 00:56:42,160
-Master.
-Gosh…

738
00:56:43,280 --> 00:56:44,640
Forgive me, I beg of you.

739
00:56:44,720 --> 00:56:47,760
Should you wish to enter the capital,
I shall accompany you.

740
00:56:49,560 --> 00:56:50,400
Really?

741
00:56:50,480 --> 00:56:51,600
Yes, Master.

742
00:57:20,040 --> 00:57:22,360
That deadpan-looking lord
says it's dangerous.

743
00:57:23,480 --> 00:57:25,800
It's not dangerous at all. It's gorgeous.

744
00:57:27,440 --> 00:57:30,080
The people here
seem kind and friendly too.

745
00:57:33,160 --> 00:57:35,440
Where are the bars? I haven't seen any.

746
00:57:36,400 --> 00:57:38,400
This quarter of the market
is most lively.

747
00:57:38,480 --> 00:57:41,760
Taverns and indulgences may be found
at the mouth of the canal.

748
00:57:41,840 --> 00:57:44,720
There, the place swarms
with foreigners and rogues.

749
00:57:44,800 --> 00:57:47,520
The Lord is doubtless concerned
about that quarter.

750
00:57:49,680 --> 00:57:51,000
Chuay.

751
00:57:51,080 --> 00:57:53,120
Can you help me get to the riverbank?

752
00:57:55,040 --> 00:57:56,280
Oh, Master Klao.

753
00:57:56,960 --> 00:57:58,480
Please, don't make me worry.

754
00:58:01,200 --> 00:58:02,360
Ow!

755
00:58:02,440 --> 00:58:03,400
I'm feeling dizzy

756
00:58:04,000 --> 00:58:05,120
and queasy.

757
00:58:05,200 --> 00:58:06,400
I'm about to pass out.

758
00:58:06,480 --> 00:58:09,240
Take me to the riverbank.

759
00:58:09,320 --> 00:58:11,720
It cannot be done, Master.

760
00:58:11,800 --> 00:58:12,920
By the Lord's order.

761
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:18,560
Fine. I'll swim there then.

762
00:58:20,800 --> 00:58:22,280
Understood, Master.

763
00:58:22,360 --> 00:58:26,360
Should we approach the canal mouth,
the Lord would punish me severely.

764
00:58:26,440 --> 00:58:27,720
Sure.

765
00:58:28,680 --> 00:58:30,720
Ow! I feel lightheaded again.

766
00:58:30,800 --> 00:58:33,720
-Get me off the boat already!
-Yes, Master.

767
00:58:47,960 --> 00:58:49,080
Do you see, Master?

768
00:58:58,560 --> 00:59:00,040
Master, pray wait.

769
00:59:25,640 --> 00:59:26,600
Master.

770
00:59:29,600 --> 00:59:30,760
Master Klao.

771
00:59:31,440 --> 00:59:32,920
Venture not beyond the pier.

772
00:59:36,160 --> 00:59:37,600
This is so cool.

773
00:59:37,680 --> 00:59:38,720
Master.

774
00:59:40,360 --> 00:59:41,320
Master Klao,

775
00:59:42,160 --> 00:59:45,360
we have strayed too far from the pier.
It is best we return.

776
00:59:45,440 --> 00:59:46,960
Just a little more.

777
00:59:54,800 --> 00:59:56,040
One of these, please.

778
00:59:59,320 --> 01:00:01,920
Let's return
once we have acquired the goods.

779
01:00:07,160 --> 01:00:11,400
-Help! Help me!
-Be wary, my Lady!

780
01:00:11,480 --> 01:00:13,680
I can bear it no more! I beg of you!

781
01:00:14,920 --> 01:00:16,520
Pray, stop this!

782
01:00:17,080 --> 01:00:19,080
-Help me!
-Cease this harassment!

783
01:00:19,160 --> 01:00:20,520
Mind your own affairs!

784
01:00:20,600 --> 01:00:23,640
This matter is none of your concern.

785
01:00:23,720 --> 01:00:26,000
Meddle not, or you shall face my wrath!

786
01:00:28,240 --> 01:00:30,360
-Master. Master Klao!
-Help! Help me!

787
01:00:30,440 --> 01:00:32,640
-Master Klao.
-Out of the way.

788
01:00:33,320 --> 01:00:34,280
Trying to slip away?

789
01:00:34,360 --> 01:00:36,640
You dare escape my reach!

790
01:00:36,720 --> 01:00:38,120
Hey!

791
01:00:49,560 --> 01:00:50,520
Klao?

792
01:01:01,560 --> 01:01:02,680
You know me?

793
01:01:03,440 --> 01:01:06,040
You. You… You…

794
01:01:30,800 --> 01:01:32,640
<i>Perhaps you're unaware</i>

795
01:01:32,720 --> 01:01:34,600
you have more enemies than you know.

796
01:01:34,680 --> 01:01:35,640
Klao!

797
01:01:36,760 --> 01:01:38,440
What have you done unto my brother!

798
01:01:38,520 --> 01:01:41,000
You don't want me to talk to her
because she's weird?

799
01:01:41,080 --> 01:01:43,760
Tell Chuay to ready my vessel.

800
01:01:43,840 --> 01:01:45,280
<i>Where to?</i>

801
01:01:45,360 --> 01:01:46,400
<i>To seek the truth.</i>

802
01:01:50,360 --> 01:01:52,040
I don't want to be parted from you.
